---
description: Patterns for writing idempotent shell scripts that manage K8s/infra resources.
globs: 'k8s/**/*.sh'
alwaysApply: true
---

Make infrastructure shell scripts safe to re-run. Use these patterns instead
of their non-idempotent equivalents:

Some examples:

| Instead of                          | Use                                                                |
| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `kubectl create secret …`           | `kubectl create … --dry-run=client -o yaml \| kubectl apply -f -`  |
| `doctl kubernetes cluster create …` | Check first: `if doctl … get …; then echo exists; else create; fi` |
| `helm install …`                    | `helm upgrade --install …`                                         |
| `kubectl create namespace …`        | `kubectl create namespace … 2>/dev/null \|\| true`                 |

Add a comment explaining the mechanism when it's not obvious.
